  "description": "<p>Currently the request context resources are built from (a) the PID (and dsID) of the object and (b) the same with all parents.</p>\n\n<p>According to the XACML 2.0 spec, multiple parent lineages should be included, ie if a resource test:res is a member of test:col1 and test:col2, then we should be generating</p>\n<ul class=\"alternate\" type=\"square\">\n\t<li>test:res</li>\n\t<li>test:col1/test:res</li>\n\t<li>test:col2/test:res</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<p>Currently only a single parent lineage is calculated (using the first parent relationship discovered in the relationships).</p>\n\n<p>This would allow resources to be members of multiple collections, and to use policies from all parent collections.</p>",
